Google Maps Platform | Review the route matrix response | Routes API | Google for Developers > About the route information in the response

The API response contains an array, where each array element defines the route from one origin waypoint to one destination waypoint. These elements are RouteMatrixElements in the gRPC method or the response body in the HTTP response.

Along with the originIndex and destinationIndex properties, each element contains only basic information specific to that route, such as distanceMeters , duration , and travelAdvisory . To get more detailed information about a route, such as a polyline, use computeRoutes .

The response has the form:

