It is important to note that proximity search does not filter out results that are far from the input location—it is intended to influence the sort order of results so the most locationally relevant matches are returned first. For example, if your location is in Seattle and you type Mount Ver , the first suggestion in the list is Mount Vernon, Washington, United States. The second is Mount Vernon, Westchester County, New York, United States. Even though Mount Vernon in New York is far from Seattle, it is still returned because it is the second most relevant candidate based on its distance from the location and its rank. To limit suggestions to a specific area, use the search Extent parameter.

