Geoapify | How to Identify Administrative Areas Along a Route | Geoapify > Read areas and crossing positions

For a single-leg GeoJSON route, read features[0].properties.admin_areas as the indexed list of countries and states or regions. country_code and state_code are lower case; country_text and state_text provide display names when available. The feature's country_code array gives the distinct countries on the route without the state-level detail.

Each admin_area_crossings item points from one entry in admin_areas to another. begin_shape_index and end_shape_index refer to positions in features[0].geometry.coordinates[0] , the route's first line. Use the coordinates at those positions to locate the transition on a map. Route step admin_area arrays identify the areas touched by a step; a step covering a boundary can contain more than one index.

For a route that stays within one administrative area, the crossing list is empty. For example, this short route within Dresden requests the same detail:

```
https://api.geoapify.com/v1/routing?waypoints=51.0493286,13.7381437|51.042327,13.736214&mode=drive&details=admin_areas&apiKey=YOUR_API_KEY
