Geoapify | How to Handle Unreachable Waypoints and Routing Errors | Geoapify > Check the distance in code

The following function compares each input waypoint with the route geometry and returns the waypoints that moved farther than a threshold. It works with the default GeoJSON format and the default stopover legs, where each waypoint pair has its own line:

```
// Great-circle distance in meters between two [lon, lat] points.
function distanceMeters([lon1, lat1], [lon2, lat2]) {
  const r = 6371008.8;
  const toRad = (d) => (d * Math.PI) / 180;
  const dLat = toRad(lat2 - lat1);
  const dLon = toRad(lon2 - lon1);
  const a = Math.sin(dLat / 2) ** 2 +
    Math.cos(toRad(lat1)) * Math.cos(toRad(lat2)) * Math.sin(dLon / 2) ** 2;
  return 2 * r * Math.asin(Math.sqrt(a));
}

// inputs: [{ lat, lon }, ...] in the order sent to the API.
function findMovedWaypoints(routeGeoJson, inputs, maxMeters = 250) {
  const lines = routeGeoJson.features[0].geometry.coordinates;
  const routed = lines.map((line) => line[0]);
  routed.push(lines[lines.length - 1].at(-1));

return inputs
    .map((input, index) => ({
      index,
      input,
      routed: routed[index],
      meters: Math.round(distanceMeters([input.lon, input.lat], routed[index]))
    }))
    .filter((item) => item.meters > maxMeters);
}
```

Geoapify | How to Handle Unreachable Waypoints and Routing Errors | Geoapify > Choose the next action in code

Classify a failed response once and map it to one action. The following JavaScript function reads statusCode and message and returns what the application should do:

```
// Returns { action, reason } for a Routing API error response.
function classifyRoutingError(status, body) {
  const message = body?.message ?? "";

if (status === 429 || status >= 500) {
    return { action: "retry", reason: "temporary" };
  }
  if (status === 401) {
    return { action: "fix-config", reason: "invalid-api-key" };
  }
  if (message.startsWith("Too long distance between locations")) {
    return { action: "split-or-change-mode", reason: "distance-limit" };
  }
  if (message.startsWith("No suitable edges near location")) {
    return { action: "move-pin", reason: "no-road-nearby" };
  }
  if (message.startsWith("No path could be found")) {
    return { action: "relax-avoid-or-change-mode", reason: "no-connection" };
  }
  // Missing or malformed waypoints, unknown mode, and other input errors.
  return { action: "fix-request", reason: "invalid-input" };
}
```

Match the beginning of the message, not the full text, because the distance message includes numbers. Swapped latitude and longitude also produce No suitable edges near location , so keep coordinates in named lat / lon fields in your code before relying on the move-pin action. Keep the final branch as a fallback for messages your code does not recognize.

